{
  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_20' aria-label=\" UV Asset Reconstruction Company Limited versus Electrosteel Castings Limited  pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('20','2026','2026_1_130_140','2026INSC14'); ><font size='4'> <strong>UV ASSET RECONSTRUCTION COMPANY LIMITED<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>ELECTROSTEEL CASTINGS LIMITED  </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 1 S.C.R. 130</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 14</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000062026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SANJAY KUMAR<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue pertains to the interpretation of Clause 2.2 of Deed of Undertaking executed between SREI-original creditor, which subsequently assigned all its rights and interests in favour of the appellant; ESL-borrower; and ECL-erstwhile promoter of ESL and obligor in and whether Clause 2.2 constitutes a contract of guarantee within the meaning of s.126 of the Contract Act, 1872 thereby rendering ECL as a guarantor to SREI in respect of financial facilities availed by ESL from SREI. Headnotes&dagger; Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016 &ndash;<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-01-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 9701/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('20','2026','2026_1_130_140','2026INSC14','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='